Planex palette_afford — Line 1 real-app evidence (v0.7)
========================================================
Zero raw-coordinate callbacks: every click routes through
the AFFORDS query. px_app_desc.on_click is NULL by design.

[1] click swatch-green (95, 34)...
    selected: green (label-routed, zero coordinate branches)

[2] click canvas twice (100,150) (150,160)...
    dots: 2, color: green (x/y consumed as payload DATA)

[3] right-click canvas (120, 140)...
    context clear: dots=0 (button-3 discriminated in the
    payload — the routing layer never branched on it)

[4] undo (graph snapshot)...
    dots restored: 2

[5] drag slider 14 -> 75 (tap/drag split by measure)...
    committed brightness: 75 (live preview reads: 40,
    estimate writes during 40-sample drag: 1)

[6] undo (brightness back to 50)...
    brightness: 50

[7] click reset (275, 34)...
    state reset via closure (undoable like any act)

[8] click empty space (40, 5)...
    no-op: no region there, no fallback handler exists

[9] keyboard: Tab ring walk (5 focusable, slider excluded)...
    ring: swatch-red, green, blue, canvas, reset (wrap OK)
    brightness NOT on the ring — no discrete affordance

[10] keyboard: Enter on swatch-blue...
    selected: blue — the SAME closure as [1], one act,
    two channels, zero coordinate branches

[11] keyboard: Shift-Tab backward...
    focus: blue -> green (reverse walk)

[12] keyboard: Enter on canvas (position-free act)...
    canvas cleared by keyboard — no dot landed because
    no position exists in a key intent (payload shape)

[13] keyboard: Tab to reset, Enter...
    state reset via keyboard (Space — the second
    activation key, same compile path)

Final state: sel=0 brightness=50 dots=0
Semantic estimate writes (whole session): 13
Raw-coordinate callbacks defined: 0 (on_click == NULL)
Unresolved clicks (no-op path): 1
Focus moves (keyboard session): 12

=== Line 1 evidence complete ===
ADR-0017 admission bar (ADR-0011) — what this app shows:
  1. Routing: 5 affordances, 1 rule, 0 coordinate branches
  2. Value: px_pointer_intent survives capture + replay
     (label embedded — see tests/test_v07.c a3)
  3. Real-app shape: acts are closures, undo through the
     graph, drag is a process with derived live preview
  4. TWO channels, one graph (v0.8 Line 1): pointer and
     keyboard compile through the same AFFORDS edges to
     the same closures — the channel is a projection
     (see tests/test_v08.c d1)
